SUMMARY:Your DC Moment | Dinner with Ambassador and Professor Lee Feinstein
DESCRIPTION:Attend an exclusive working dinner and strategy session for t
 he Spring 2027 D.C. Global Policy Program. Don't just study global leader
 ship. Put it into practice.  This intimate event is for students interest
 ed in the Hamilton Lugar Spring 2027 residency. It's a working dinner and
  a peek at what a global career actually feels like before you step into 
 it.Why you should attend:Sit at the Table: Engage with a leader who has s
 haped global policy and his international career.  Alumni Insights: Hear 
 from a panel of D.C. Program alumni regarding their on-the-ground experie
 nces.  The Professional Roadmap: Get a technical walkthrough of the Sprin
 g 2027 cycle\, including the January 11 – May 7 residency dates.  Logis
 tics Bridge: Understand how the IU Capital Campus housing works and how t
 he classes work for undergrads\, grad\, and PhD students.  The AgendaI. T
