SUMMARY:Global Competencies Series: Student Career Dinner & Fireside Chat
  with Veteran Humanitarian Paula Reed Lynch
DESCRIPTION:Kick off theGlobal Competencies Skills Development Serieswith
  an exclusive\, small-group evening networking dinner and candid career c
 onversation featuring Foreign Service veteran and former Senior Executive
  Service (SES) leaderPaula Reed Lynch. Drop by. You do not have to stay f
 or the whole event. Open to all staff\, faculty\, students\, and the publ
 ic.Moving beyond standard Q&amp\;A panels\, this dinner offers students d
 irect access to a top international policy leader who managed over$4 Bill
 ionin global humanitarian aid and led UN delegations. Enjoy a catered din
 ner while discussing high-impact career pathways in international affairs
 \, government service\, global NGOs\, and multilateral diplomacy.What You
 'll Get Out of It (Why Attend?)Direct Access &amp\; Mentorship:Engage in 
 an intimate roundtable setting with a seasoned executive who served nearl
 y five decades on the front lines of U.S. foreign policy.Unfiltered Caree
 r Insights:Ask your real questions about navigating Foreign Service caree
 rs\, policy integration across USAID &amp\; the Department of State\, and
  entry points into global non-profit sectors.High-Impact Networking:Conne
 ct with student leaders\, fellowship recipients\, and peers across HLS\, 
 O'Neill\, Cybersecurity\, and Public Policy majors.Key NACE Competencies 
 Addressed:Career &amp\; Self-Development\, Professionalism\, Communicatio
 n\, and Equity &amp\; Inclusion.  Meet the Guest Speaker - Paula Reed Lyn
 chspent nearly five decades on the front lines of U.S. foreign policy and
  international relief.Serving 14 years in the Senior Executive Service wi
 thin the Department of State's Bureau of Population\, Refugees\, and Migr
 ation (PRM)\, Paula oversaw budgets exceeding $4 billion for global disas
